    kg:docId "1012.2599v1_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1012_2599v1_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan ", 2009], a process sometimes called intensication . Nonstationary noise models are also possible, such as autoregressive moving-average noise [Murray-Smith and Girard, 2001] and heteroskedastic Gaussian noise [Goldberg et al. , 1998]. 2.5 A brief history of Bayesian optimization The earliest work we are aware of resembling the modern Bayesian optimization approach is the early work of Kushner [1964], who used Wiener processes for unconstrained one-dimensional problems. Kushners decision model wa" .

