    kg:textSpan "Reduction Algorithms The increasing amount of collected data provides ample information, but also increases problem complexity. In real-world applications, many features are irrelevant or redundant to predict target variables. Dimensionality reduction algorithms often serve as feature engineering methods to extract important features and eliminate insignicant or redundant features. Two common dimensionality-reduction algorithms are principal component analysis (PCA) and linear discriminant analy" .

