    kg:textSpan "compatibility particularly problematic because networks that compute the same function can appear very different. However, because NEAT has a solution to the competing conventions problem, using historical information about genes, the population in NEAT can easily be speciated. We use explicit tness sharing , which forces individuals with similar genomes to share their tness payoff (Goldberg and Richardson, 1987). The original implicit version of tness sharing introduced by Holland (1975) groupe" .

