        "CQ_S0_R1_0237"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceChunk "1810.13306_rag::chunk_025"^^xsd:string,
        "1906.02287_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "1906.02287_rag::chunk_014"^^xsd:string,
        "2008.08516_rag::chunk_005"^^xsd:string,
        "2008.08516_rag::chunk_012"^^xsd:string,
        "5872-efficient-and-robust-automated-machine-learning_rag::chunk_004"^^xsd:string,
        "A_Imbrea_AutoML_Data_Streams_rag::chunk_001"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "Meta-learning procedures already perform a sort of transfer learning, however, a promising research venue is to transfer knowledge on information on the optimization process"^^xsd:string,
        "This approach of warmstarting optimization by meta-learning has already been successfully applied before"^^xsd:string,
        "When other techniques from the general eld of AutoML, such as meta-learning, are needed, it is specically mentioned."^^xsd:string,
        "a meta-learning approach where the meta-features of the input dataset is extracted and compared with the meta-features of the datasets that are stored in the frameworks knowledge base"^^xsd:string,
        "congurations based on meta-learning and use their result to seed Bayesian optimization."^^xsd:string,
        "meta-learning by itself can be seen as an AutoML methodology: early approaches were used to make coarse model suggestions to solve supervised learning problems"^^xsd:string,
        "meta-learning can be described as the process of learning from previous experience gained during applying various learning algorithms on dierent kinds of data"^^xsd:string,
        "utilizes meta-learning to facilitate rapid transfer across tasks"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Meta-learning"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "An approach where meta-features of an input dataset are extracted and compared with stored datasets to identify best performing algorithms."^^xsd:string ;
