    kg:textSpan "can be optimized for each layer are also limited. Furthermore, the computations are extremely heavy; to generate the final best network, many thousands of candidate architectures have to be evaluated and trained, which requires hundreds of thousands of GPU hours. An alternative direction for architecture search is evolutionary algorithms (EAs). They are well suited for this problem because they are black-box optimization algorithms that can optimize arbitrary structure. Some of these approaches " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1906_02287_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
