    kg:textSpan "b = B/n ). Successive halving serves as a subroutine on each set of random congurations to eliminate the poorly-performing hyper-parameter congurations and improve eciency. The main steps of Hyperband algorithms are shown in Algorithm 1 [2]. Algorithm 1 Hyperband Input: b max , b min 1: s max = log b max b min 2: for s { b max , b min 1 , . . . , 0 } do 3: n = DetermineBudget ( s ) 4: = SampleConfigurations ( n ) 5: SuccessiveHalving ( ) 6: end for 7: return The best conguration so far. Firstly," .

